  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Production of nutritious snack pellet</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Note: This project has been cancelled, because the applicant is no longer confident that the PSI project can be implemented and completed in time, because of delays caused by issues between shareholders of the local partner.There is a growing concern about the effect of snack food on children in the Palestinian Territories. The Palestinian Ministry of Education issued new food regulations in 2008 that effectively ban the sale of snacks in school canteens unless they meet certain minimum nutritional values that no local producer so far is able to meet. The partners have the intention to introduce the production of fat-free snack pellets to the Palestinian Territories, Israel and nearby countries and support their clients in product formulation, nutritional values and quality aspects. The main ingredient of the snack pellets will be corn instead of potato, the pellets will be fortified with fibres and protein for added nutrition and expanded by hot air instead of oil.The applicant, the Italian company FEN s.r.l., designs and manufactures state-of-the-art machines to produce a wide range of products such as snack pellets, pasta, baby foods and breakfast cereals. They also supply technology and know-how to snack producers worldwide. FEN s.r.l. is established in 1991 and currently employs 23 persons.The local partner Al-Qasrawi Industrial &amp; Trade Co. Ltd is the only snack pellet producer in the Palestinian territories. The company is established in 1992 and employs 170 persons. The two companies will set up a joint venture for this project in Hebron. The joint venture&apos;s production will be ISO 22000 and Kosher certified.</narrative>
  </description>
